From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:22:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/41] server: the max-min prompt share divides the pass
 budget, not its running rest (LLAMA_SERVER_SHARE_PASS_BUDGET=0: off)

share_prompt_budget's sharing loop computed each slot's share from the
running `budget`, which the earlier slots of the same pass had already
reduced: with skew 1 two equal prompts got 682 + 1365 of a 2047-token window
(not 1024 + 1023, the documented plain max-min share).  A hybrid model's
split_equal then cut such a step into short ubatches (512, 512, 340, 512,
171 instead of 4 x 512).  The share now divides budget_before; floors still
sum to at most budget_before, and the no-progress exit is unchanged.

Found and Fable-reviewed in the rdna3 session (7900 XTX: Inkling -8 %,
Qwen3.6-35B -1.8 % within noise).  R9700 prod config (Flash-Next, -sm tensor,
.r366a env), two fresh prompts prefilled at once: 39K + 34K 27.5 -> 22.7 s,
59K + 59K 44.7 -> 37.3 s (-17 %); single requests unchanged (greedy, the
512-token prompt set).  Concurrent replies change with the ubatch shape in
both arms (each matches the prompts-alone run on 2 of 4).
---
 tools/server/server-context.cpp | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
index 6f5b336404..d5759e9e7d 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -1202,6 +1202,12 @@ private:
     // every step (and so still gives feedback), and the rest accelerate as slots retire.  Any value >= 1 keeps
     // starvation impossible.  1 is the plain max-min share and allocates EXACTLY what it did before this knob
     // existed, so the equal-share measurements stay valid.
+    // LLAMA_SERVER_SHARE_PASS_BUDGET (on unless 0): share_prompt_budget divides each pass's budget, not its running rest
+    const bool share_pass_budget = [] {
+        const char * e = getenv("LLAMA_SERVER_SHARE_PASS_BUDGET");
+        return e == nullptr || atoi(e) != 0;
+    }();
+
     const int32_t prefill_skew = [] {
         const char * e = getenv("LLAMA_SERVER_PREFILL_SKEW");
         if (e == nullptr) {
@@ -2529,7 +2535,10 @@ private:
             for (size_t i = 0; i < active.size(); ++i) {
                 const size_t  k = active[i];
                 const int64_t w = (i == skew_i ? prefill_skew : 1);
-                const int64_t share_i = (int64_t) budget * w / wsum;
+                // a share of the pass's budget (budget_before), not of what the earlier slots of this pass left over:
+                // with `budget` two equal prompts got 1/3 and 2/3 of the window (682 + 1365 of 2047), and a hybrid
+                // model's split_equal then cut the step into short ubatches.  LLAMA_SERVER_SHARE_PASS_BUDGET=0: the old share
+                const int64_t share_i = (int64_t) (share_pass_budget ? budget_before : budget) * w / wsum;
                 const int64_t take    = std::min<int64_t>(remaining[k], share_i);
 
                 prompt_budget[k] += (int32_t) take;
